[I] HTTP cookie jars

[T] HTTP::Cookies is a Perl class for objects that represent a cookie jar, a
[T] database of all HTTP cookies a user agent knows about. It can add cookie
[T] headers to requests, extract cookies from responses and save and load
[T] them from files, and is used by LWP::UserAgent.

[U] https://metacpan.org/dist/HTTP-Cookies

